<% title = 'Meridian — Incident management for teams that ship' %>
<div class="mdn-hero mb-5">
  <h1 class="display-6 fw-semibold mb-3">Incident response, status pages, and partner integrations in one place.</h1>
  <p class="lead mb-4">Meridian helps mid-size engineering teams track incidents, keep customers informed with a public status page, and connect their tooling through a partner API.</p>
  <a class="btn btn-light btn-lg me-2" href="/register">Get started</a>
  <a class="btn btn-outline-light btn-lg" href="/status">View status page</a>
</div>

<div class="row g-4">
  <div class="col-md-4">
    <div class="mdn-card p-4 h-100">
      <h2 class="h5">Incident tracking</h2>
      <p class="text-muted mb-0">Log incidents, assign severity, and keep a searchable history of postmortems across your organization.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-4">
    <div class="mdn-card p-4 h-100">
      <h2 class="h5">Public status pages</h2>
      <p class="text-muted mb-0">Give customers visibility into platform health with a hosted status page and email subscriptions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-4">
    <div class="mdn-card p-4 h-100">
      <h2 class="h5">Partner integrations</h2>
      <p class="text-muted mb-0">Connect webhook relays and downstream tooling through the Meridian Partner Integration Platform, powered by GraphQL.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
